@{
    // This is the "V" in MVC: the View.
    // The controller decides which page to open, and this file decides how that page looks.
    // ViewData is a dictionary that can pass simple values from the controller to the view.
    // In this case, the page title is set so the browser tab and layout can use it.
    ViewData["Title"] = "Hello";
}

@*
    This Razor file is a .cshtml page. It mixes HTML with C# code.
    When a browser requests the Hello page, the controller calls this view,
    and the browser renders the HTML you see here.

    MVC stands for Model-View-Controller:
    - Model: data and business logic
    - View: what the user sees on the page
    - Controller: handles requests and decides which view to show
*@

<h1>Hello World</h1>
<p>Welcome to the Hello controller view.</p>
